+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every registered tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry` enforces that same schema before any tool executor runs. Rejecting malformed input at the registry boundary gives every tool one predictable failure contract without requiring hand-written validation inside each executor.
+
+## Execution contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` (enforcing `required`, declared property types, and `enum` without coercing types) before calling the executor; on failure it never invokes the executor, returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing property paths and constraints, and omits every input property value from both `result` and emitted log entries ([validated by: rejects invalid input without invoking the executor or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, `ChatOrchestrator` forwards the failure description to the provider as a `tool_result` within the existing `maxToolRounds` loop so the model can correct its call, and valid input passes through to the executor unchanged — preserving unlisted extra properties without injecting schema defaults ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back to the model so a retry succeeds with extra keys intact](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L129)).
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` continues to throw `Unknown tool: <name>` when given an unregistered tool name, reserving thrown exceptions for unknown tools while returning `ToolResponse` objects for schema rejections.
+
+## Schema compilation and resolution
+
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` during `ToolRegistry.register` and throws an error naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled, failing at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static schema is invalid](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L75)).
+- Registering a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves the definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned on that call rather than freezing the registration-time schema ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against each call current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L90)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration and reused across repeated `execute` calls, while a function-valued tool caches compiled validators by the resolved schema object reference.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Changing `Unknown tool: <name>` from a thrown exception to a returned `ToolResponse` is tracked separately because it alters direct callers of `ToolRegistry.execute`.
+- Validating tool output, hallucination detection, per-tool authorization, `beforeToolCall` veto hooks, and retry, timeout, or rate-limiting policies around tool execution are outside this specification.
